    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0368" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/1258½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State ad interim</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">14 June, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I think that this
                        despatch<anchor n="79" xml:id="d257-f1"/> ought to be sent. Every word of it
                    is true.</p>
                <p>But Colonel House, who comes direct from London, landed in New York yesterday
                    from the <hi rendition="#italic">Saint Paul;</hi> and, if a delay of a day or
                    two would not be imprudent, I think we had better wait to get his advice. He is
                    well informed, I happen to know on these very matters and has himself been
                    advising the British Foreign Office of our attitude.</p>
                <p>Cordially Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="79" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Draft telegram, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
